  "raw_text": "our top two or three factors, such as taste, portion size, speed, nutrition, consistency, or price, and explain how you judge if something is \"worth it\"? User: I would say if it fills me up and it's a reasonable price, it's a good value. McDonald's has a value meal now where it's a double cheeseburger and nuggets and fries and a drink for $5. And I think that's a really good value because $5 is pretty cheap these days for a whole meal. Agent: That's a very clear definition of good value for you: feeling full for a reasonable price, and you've given a great example with the five-dollar meal. Now, thinking about the past two weeks, what have been your most common fast-food patterns? This includes when you eat it, what you usually order, and what typically triggers those choices. User: I've actually cut back a lot on eating fast food just because the prices keep going up. And, I mean, not just with fast food, with everything, so we have less money. So I haven't been going to fast food as",
